    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test passed, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the E.164 national-number length check against country code in `E164Telephone.normalize` \u2014 the single point where the telephone is cleaned and its country code / national digits are resolved.\n\n**Change:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`\n\nAfter the existing generic 8\u201315 total-digit sanity check, it now resolves the country code by longest-matching prefix (`61` \u2192 9 national digits, `1` \u2192 10) and throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (which the existing handler maps to **400**) when the national number isn't exactly the required length for that country. Unrecognized country codes keep the prior generic behavior.\n\nVerification of the key cases:\n- `+61 123` \u2192 `61123`, national `123` (3 digits) \u2260 9 \u2192 **400** (the new test's expectation).\n- `uniqueTelephone()` `04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits \u2192 accepted, so all valid-owner payloads across the suite still pass.\n\nThe targeted test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` and the full suite both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
